Colleague errors: several mis-map pal4 to "plot 4" instead of plot5; some claim ocean.balance has insufficient L separation, others say it does; duplicate 20 in pal4 noted as potential flaw by several. 

Consensus emerging on varying-L palettes (pal1 or pal4) being only viable candidates; no one claims const-L palettes work. Unresolved: whether ocean.balance's L steps are truly distinct enough for 5 categories vs. pal4's explicit but duplicated samples. My prior view aligns with plot5 (pal4) as strongest due to explicit L variation.}

